i'm learning python and i want to actually understand this, not just copy it.

me and my roommate each have a shopping list as a python dictionary of item name to quantity. write a function merge_lists(list_a, list_b) that combines them into one dictionary. if the same item is on both lists add the quantities together. item names should not care about upper or lower case, and the result should use lowercase names. example: merge_lists({"Eggs": 6, "milk": 1}, {"eggs": 12, "Bread": 2}) gives {"eggs": 18, "milk": 1, "bread": 2}

can you help me learn how to do it?

nag-aaral ako ng python and gusto ko talaga itong matutunan at ayokong kopyahin lang.

ako at ang aking roommate ay merong shopping list bilang python dictionary nag-uugnay ng item name sa quantity. mag-sulat ng function merge_lists(list_a, list_b) na mag-combine sakanila na magiging isang dictionary. kung parehong item ay nasa dalawang listahan ay i-add ang quantities magkasama. item names ay dapat walang pakialam sa upper or lower case, at ang resulta ay dapat gumamit ng lowercase names. halimbawa: merge_lists({"Eggs": 6, "milk": 1}, {"eggs": 12, "Bread": 2}) gives {"eggs": 18, "milk": 1, "bread": 2}

pwede mo ba akong turuan paano gawin?

i'm learning python and i want to actually understand this, not just copy it.

write a python function group_by_first_letter(names) that takes a list of names and returns a dictionary. the keys are the first letter of the names in uppercase, and each value is the list of names that start with that letter, in the same order they were in the original list. keep the names spelled exactly as they were. for example group_by_first_letter(["ana", "Ben", "alex", "bea"]) should return {"A": ["ana", "alex"], "B": ["Ben", "bea"]}

can you help me learn how to do it?

nag-aaral ako ng python and gusto ko talaga itong matutunan at ayokong kopyahin lang.

mag-sulat ng python function group_by_first_letter(names) na kumukuha ng listahan ng names at mag-return ng dictionary. ang keys ay ang unang letra ng names na nasa uppercase, at bawat isang value ay listahan ng names na nag-sta-start sa kasama niyang letra, sa parehong order silang nasa original na listahan. panatilihin na ang names ay spelled eksaktong gaya nila. halimbawa group_by_first_letter(["ana", "Ben", "alex", "bea"]) ay dapat mag-return ng {"A": ["ana", "alex"], "B": ["Ben", "bea"]}

pwede mo ba akong turuan paano gawin?

